From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: npu: assign the coherent DMA pool

NPU V2 can only address host DRAM at 0x80000000-0xbfffffff; higher
addresses alias the lower 1 GiB. Coherent buffers dereferenced by the
NPU, the mailbox buffers and the mt76 WLAN rings, must stay in that
window.

Assign the optional "dma" shared-dma-pool to the NPU device before the
mailbox buffers are allocated. Streaming mappings are not affected:
packet buffers are only passed through to the WLAN DMA engine.

Co-authored-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -717,6 +717,11 @@ static const struct regmap_config regmap
 	.disable_locking	= true,
 };
 
+static void airoha_npu_release_dma_pool(void *dev)
+{
+	of_reserved_mem_device_release(dev);
+}
+
 static int airoha_npu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
@@ -800,6 +805,17 @@ static int airoha_npu_probe(struct platf
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
+	/*
+	 * NPU V2 can only address the first 1 GiB of DRAM: place coherent
+	 * buffers shared with the NPU in the "dma" pool, if provided.
+	 */
+	err = of_reserved_mem_device_init_by_name(dev, dev->of_node, "dma");
+	if (!err)
+		err = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, airoha_npu_release_dma_pool,
+					       dev);
+	if (err && err != -ENODEV)
+		return err;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(npu->cores); i++) {
 		struct airoha_npu_core *core = &npu->cores[i];
 
